# Renesas/Dialog DA145xx SDK6. Licensed, marked "Confidential Information",
# and gated behind a Renesas account. Download it yourself; see
# firmware/hema_epd_clock/BUILD_AND_FLASH.md.
SDK_6.0.22.1401/
SDK_*.zip
DA145xx_SDK/

# Renesas e² studio installer (~1.8 GB).
e2studio_installer*.run

# Waveshare/vendor STM32 EPD reference demo, used only as a driver reference.
STM32-F103ZET6/
STM32-F103ZET6.zip

# Vendor ESL firmware images (proprietary binaries — reference only).
*.bin
*.img
firmware_archive/

# Vendor documentation transcribed from their login-gated site.
function_doc_official.txt

# Vendor web control tool, mirrored for protocol analysis.
webpage/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reverse-engineering scratch work
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ghidra_project/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.o
*.d
*.elf
*.hex
*.map
*.lst
DA14585/
DA14531/
Debug/
Release/

# Eclipse / e² studio local state (the tracked .project/.cproject are
# generated by tools/gen_e2studio_project.py and are intentionally kept).
.metadata/
.settings/
*.launch

# Self-signed TLS certificate + private key generated by webui/serve.py. Local
# to one machine and one LAN address, so there is nothing to share.
webui/.certs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
debug.png

# Full-size originals of the phone photos. Downscaled copies of the ones worth
# keeping are committed under docs/img/.
IMG_*.jpg
test*.jpg
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Unmodified SDK Keil template, kept locally but not published: it does not
# have src/epd/*.c wired in, so shipping it would be a broken build config.
# Build with e² studio (tools/gen_e2studio_project.py).
firmware/hema_epd_clock/Keil_5/

# Community-sourced J-Link device definition plus Dialog's jtag_programmer flash
# algorithm. Vendor binaries — redistributed from neither Renesas nor the
# community author. Install into /opt/SEGGER/JLink yourself; see the local
# BUILD_AND_FLASH.md.
Jflash-replacement-file/

# Documentation is kept local while development is in progress. The full
# write-up (protocol notes, build/flash guide, GPIO tracing) gets rewritten and
# published once the firmware is feature-complete; until then only the top-level
# README is tracked, so the public repo cannot drift out of date.
PROTOCOL_NOTES.md
firmware/hema_epd_clock/BUILD_AND_FLASH.md
firmware/hema_epd_clock/GPIO_TRACING_GUIDE.md
firmware/hema_epd_clock/README.md
docs/
